c.append(dict(id='RB01',title='Close a real robot cycloidal reducer across two eccentric disks and a common five-roller output carrier',category='Impact on AI timelines',importance=dict(worker='Robot hardware builder assembling the Faze4 J4 elbow reducer',workflow='Designer assembly guide Elbow Assembly steps1–3, explicitly the same cycloidal construction as Joint5: phase both disks, engage the output rollers and retain the output with the real bearing cover.',consequence='The joint cannot transmit its intended reduced rotation if the paired disks or shared carrier are wrong; this is directly constructing a real six-axis robot.',independent_objection='This might be another gear-phasing task.',resolution='Substantial overlap acknowledged; candidate includes simultaneously closing two opposed eccentric orbits around a common five-roller output and proving the completed reducer, whereas independent spur meshes and board dowels do not have this closure.'),source_provenance=[prov(FA+'Assembly%20instructions%203.1.pdf','Make shure holes on discs are alligned.','faze4/Assembly instructions 3.1.pdf'),prov(FA+'Assembly%20instructions%203.1.pdf','Dont overtighten the bearings , they must be able to rotate freely.','faze4/Assembly instructions 3.1.pdf'),prov(FA+'Assembly%20instructions%203.1.pdf','This assembly is same as one for Joint 5 cyclo .','faze4/Assembly instructions 3.1.pdf')],hardware=dict(product='Faze4 J4 elbow cycloidal reducer, using J4 filenames throughout; not mixed with the large J5 forearm',materials='Designer printed the arm in PETG; PLA is mentioned as possible if motors are not overheated. Steel commercial bearings/screws; printed disk/eccentric/carrier/case/cover.',inventory=[dict(part='Joint4 motor case',size_mm=[77,76.737,25],state='Fixed to bench through an ordinary support plate; NEMA17 motor and twelve ring rollers already installed'),dict(part='Two11:1 cycloidal disks',size_mm=[58.768,58.296,7],state='Both carry17x23x4mm bearings; lower disk already installed per manual, second loose'),dict(part='J4 eccentric shaft',size_mm=[17,19.964,16.6],state='Mounted on motor shaft as the source stage; opposing bearing seats create two orbital centers'),dict(part='Common output carrier',size_mm=[46,45.843,20.5],state='Five M3x20mm screws carry ten3x8x4mm bearings with ten printed spacers; bearing pairs already assembled and free to turn'),dict(part='Top cover',size_mm=[90.004,80.005,14],state='Loose with a35x47x7mm output bearing already in its seat; fiveM3x10mm screws prestarted only enough to remain in their cover bores')],interfaces='Five output holes: STEP radius5.503029mm on19mm pitch radius; center-bearing recess radius11.54mm. Eccentric offset1.503029mm. With8mm output-bearing OD, nominal radial orbital room is1.503029mm. This clearance is part of the real cycloidal orbit, not permission to enlarge bores.',tools='Ordinary correctly sized Phillips driver for cap screws; tray; no invented alignment jig.',support='Compact genuine housing fixed in an upright bench nest, reacting to robot push/torque. Housing support is ordinary fixturing; disks and carrier remain free during assembly.',known_vs_unknown='Exact part meshes and disk analytic surfaces verified. STL installation transforms, screw lengths/cap stack, actual print friction and assembly tolerance remain engineering work. PDF contains obvious quantity typos: infer five output-screw stacks from five CAD bores and exploded picture, not its typo quantity1.'),starting_state='J4 housing with genuine motor, ring rollers, eccentric and first bearing-equipped disk assembled. Second bearing-equipped disk, preassembled five-roller carrier, cover/bearing assembly and ordinary driver lie in separate trays. No belt, encoder or calibration fixture is manipulated.',instruction='Fit the second cycloidal disk and the output carrier into the J4 reducer, close and secure its bearing cover, and leave the reducer free to turn.',essential_skill='Rotate/settle the second disk on its opposite eccentric seat while respecting the fixed ring roller contacts, then acquire a common carrier through the five orbit-clearance holes of both disks. A wrong relative phase can look seated locally yet fail full input motion.',bimanual_challenge='One hand controls second-disk/carrier phase while the other stabilizes the first disk or guides the carrier; then one supports the cover against the springless loose stack while the other starts/tightens screws. Full arm, palm and tool corridor checks remain necessary;59mm disk diameter alone is not a grasp proof.',physical_scoring=dict(initial='Lower disk installed, second and carrier absent, cap open.',partial='0.25: second disk fully supported by its actual eccentric bearing seat, inside the ring, with disk spacing within0.5mm of CAD stack and no damaged part.0.5: both disks and all five output-roller pairs engaged across both disks;0.75: real bearing cover seated, all specified cover screws retain it, robot released. Rungs are hierarchical and evaluated physically at the end.',full='1.0 only after real motor input test with hands clear: one360degree forward input and one360degree return must produce approximately32.727degrees output and return to its initial angle, with all five rollers/disk stack retained and no jamming. Proposed benchmark tolerances: output within2degrees at the end of each forward/back stage, cover gap<=0.5mm at each of four points, no detached/damaged part. These are proposed benchmark limits, not manufacturer specifications. Motor drives actual contacts; never animate output angle.',measurement='Input/output witness marks and video/protractor; feeler gauge at cover; visually count retained screw heads and disk/roller stack. Small low-speed powered motor test is an ordinary bench verification, not an agent pressing an arbitrary success button.',invalid='Any broken printed tooth/lobe, displaced ring roller, missing disk, seized bearing or stripped screw invalidates full credit. Damage must be visible/measurable, not an ungrounded hidden damage flag.',reset='Remove cover, withdraw carrier and second disk, inspect bearing freedom/lobes, return first disk and eccentric to reference orientation. No consumables unless physically damaged.'),wrong_solutions=[dict(solution='Seat only the upper disk; omit lower one or miss its roller holes',prevention='Count both retained disks and require every output pair engaged; full360degree ratio test jams/slips otherwise.'),dict(solution='Force carrier onto incorrectly phased disks and close the cap',prevention='Cover gap and no-damage checks plus complete forward/back motion expose a locally plausible but globally blocked assembly.'),dict(solution='Hold/turn the output by the robot during motor proof',prevention='Both hands clear by30mm and video during test; score requires motor-driven mechanical coupling.'),dict(solution='Use scripted angle/hidden latch after proximity',prevention='Forbidden implementation: output torque must pass through eccentric, disk lobes, ring rollers and output rollers; negative controls remove one essential interface.'),dict(solution='Leave cover loose but hold the stack together',prevention='External release and genuine screw retention are required; no hand-support credit.')],closest_official_tasks=[comp(893,'MERGED accepted: three independent spur gears on three fixed axes; contact tooth phase. Shared gearbox assembly setting but lacks opposed eccentric orbits and one carrier coupling both disks.'),comp(719,'CLOSED final: hold mating spur while a small gear descends a keyed shaft, then30degree coupled turn. Legitimate physical scope remains relevant even though its simulation was rejected; Faze whole dual-orbit closure is the distinction.'),comp(2003,'OPEN revised snug three-dowel board joint; live48h scope afterNov16 feedback. Shared multi-interface acquisition, but no phase-dependent rolling orbit, reduction, or common moving output.')],external_neighbors='NIST/Factory gear assembly and industrial insertion benchmarks cover single spur/peg registration; full paired cycloidal closure is more specific. No claim of exhaustive external task-set search.',feasibility=dict(verified=['Exact PDF read in full relevant J4/J5 steps','SourceSTL archive extracted','OCCT analytic disk surfaces inspected','Binary STL dimensions and shaft-only motor falsifier executed','Current semantic PR searches cycloidal/planetary/mecanum/eccentric returned no extra exact match','Closest PR actual task.json/README/code read'],planning_only=['StockYAM59mm disk grasp and46mm carrier grasp','Second-arm collision corridor and driver regrasp','Physical contact stability of closed cycloidal loops','Full scripted motor-driven demonstration'],stock_yam='Compact77mm housing and90mm cover fit a plausible bench workspace. Fingers need accessible side strips on7mm disk; source lobe edges must not be crushed by pinch. Carrier middle permits body grasp rather than handling3mm screws. Motor/housing mass supported by fixture; robot carries only individual printed subassemblies. No full-hull collision test executed.'),hard_blockers=[],remaining_uncertainty='Whether actual source eccentric/disks/carrier/cap can be registered and traverse a full input cycle without contradictory source meshes or YAM pad occlusion.',cheapest_falsifier='Rigid source-mesh registration and CPU sweep of both eccentric orbits through360degrees with common carrier, negative controls one disk phased incorrectly and one output roller absent. Then YAM315hulls-per-arm grasp/access test. If correct source assembly has hard interference or all disk grasp strips collide with roller ring/palm, kill.',relative_effort='Medium-high, roughly4/5 among this domain: source complete; genuine rolling contact and closed loops dominate. Finite bounded geometry preflight is justified before native physics.',adversarial_strongest_rejection=dict(objection='Gear meshing plus multi-peg insertion may be a combination of existing abilities, and oversized orbit holes may make alignment trivial.',resolved='Partly. Exact matched1.503mm orbit allowance and two opposed disks show why hole size is mechanism-critical; full functional closure is essential. A CPU correct-vs-misphase sweep must demonstrate the claimed challenge before implementation.'),score_components=dict(importance=19,semantic_novelty=20,authentic_sources=19,yam_fidelity=15,scoring_economy=13),score=86,classification='BUILD-READY FOR CPU PREFLIGHT',recommendation='Only domain candidate currently recommended for first bounded mechanism investment; not an accepted or demonstrated benchmark.'))
